.TH LPI 1 "2026-09-23" "learning-pi" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lpi \- control the pi learning system: gated updates and the test suite
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lpi
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lpi
is the control command for the pi learning system. pi and its extension packages
are hard-pinned in
.IR ~/learning-pi/versions.lock.json ;
nothing updates itself.
.B lpi update
stages any newer pi and extension-package versions in an isolated sandbox, runs
.B "lpi test"
against that candidate set, and promotes everything only if every learning
behavior invariant still passes. On failure it stays pinned and writes a
diagnosis report. It never patches code.
.PP
.B lpi
wraps
.IR ~/learning-pi/harness/pi-safe-update " (updates)"
and
.IR ~/learning-pi/scripts/learn-check " (tests)."
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR e2e " [" \-\-scenario " " ID "] [" \-\-tier " smoke|full] [" \-\-flows " " a,b "] [" \-\-list "] [" \-\-keep "]"
Replay short learner journeys against a sandboxed pi with the real models.
Each scenario sends a real flow command
.RB ( /teach ", " /review ", " /ingest ", " /show ", " /audit )
to an isolated copy of the layer, then checks the session transcript: the
expected worker/verifier subagents must have run and finished clean, required
receipts must appear, and the final turn must not be withheld. The real
.B ~/learning-system
and
.B ~/.pi/agent
are never written. Model access (credentials, model catalog, pinned packages)
is read-only.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-scenario ID
Run only the named scenario (repeatable, or a comma list).
.TP
.B \-\-tier smoke|full
Run only scenarios of that tier. The smoke tier stops at the first meaningful
signal (the flow's key subagent plus a first clean turn) so it stays fast; the
full tier runs each flow to its natural settle (for example the ingest closing
summary) and is much slower.
.TP
.B \-\-flows a,b
Run only scenarios for those flows.
.TP
.B \-\-list
List the scenarios and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-jobs N
Run N scenarios concurrently, each in its own sandbox. Ignored when a fixed
.B \-\-sandbox
is supplied. Default 1. Higher values raise model-provider contention and make
the journeys flakier, so raise it only once the scenarios are hardened.
.TP
.B \-\-retries N
Retry a failed scenario in a fresh sandbox up to N times (default 1). Model
turn-hygiene is nondeterministic; a retry absorbs a one-off withhold without
masking a repeatable break.
.TP
.B \-\-diff-ls DIR
With
.BR \-\-diff ,
also diff this learning-system checkout (default
.IR $LEARNING_SYSTEM_ROOT " or " ~/learning-system ).
.TP
.B \-\-no-diff-ls
With
.BR \-\-diff ,
diff only the learning-pi layer.
.TP
.B \-\-keep
Keep the sandbox for inspection (otherwise it is removed).
.RE
.TP
.BR check ", " c " (default)"
Read-only. Reports the pinned and newest pi version and extension-package
versions, and scans the candidate pi changelog for changes to surfaces the
learning layer depends on.
.TP
.BR update ", " up " [\-\-to VER] [\-\-dry-run] [\-\-pi-only]"
Resolve newer pi and package versions, stage them side-by-side, run
.BR "lpi test" ,
and promote only on success. Options:
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-to VER
Use a specific pi version instead of the newest.
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Stage and test, but change nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-pi-only
Ignore extension-package updates and consider pi only.
.TP
.B \-\-e2e
Also run the end-to-end learner journeys against the candidate set before
promotion. Slow (real models); off by default.
.TP
.B \-\-e2e-flows a,b
With
.BR \-\-e2e ,
limit the journeys to those flows.
.TP
.B \-\-e2e-jobs N
With
.BR \-\-e2e ,
run N journeys concurrently (default 1).
.RE
.TP
.BR test ", " t " [\-\-with-sidecars] [\-\-no-load] [\-\-sandbox DIR]"
Run the learning-layer test suite: gate behavior and golden scenarios, resource
checks, contract coverage against
.IR contracts/learning-core.json ,
and an isolated, no-model load probe. Exits non-zero unless every invariant
passes.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-with-sidecars
Also run the learning-system
.I ops
unittest suite (read-only) against the real checkout.
.TP
.B \-\-no-load
Skip the load probe (used in CI, where no pi binary is present).
.TP
.B \-\-sandbox DIR
Run the load probe against a pre-built sandbox instead of building one.
.TP
.B \-\-e2e
Also run the end-to-end learner journeys (real models, sandboxed). Slow; off by
default. See the
.B e2e
command for the journey options.
.RE
.TP
.BR doctor ", " dr
Re-run the test suite against the currently pinned versions. Use after a
hand-run
.B pi update
to detect drift.
.TP
.BR rollback ", " rb
Restore the pi and package versions from the previous promotion recorded in the
journal.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B lpi
Show what, if anything, can be updated.
.TP
.B lpi up
Apply all available pi and extension-package updates through the gate.
.TP
.B lpi up \-\-dry-run
See whether the candidate set passes without changing anything.
.TP
.B lpi test
Reproduce a diagnosis locally.
.TP
.B lpi rb
Undo the last promotion.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, or no update was available.
.TP
.B 1
A candidate failed
.BR "lpi test" ,
the test suite failed, or an
.B lpi e2e
journey failed. The current pins were kept and a diagnosis was written.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.TP
.B 3
Staging error (could not install or build the sandbox).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/learning-pi/versions.lock.json
The pinned pi version, package versions, and the promotion journal.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/learning-pi/diagnosis-*.md
Failure diagnosis reports. Repair them with the
.B lpi
opencode skill.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/learning-pi/audit-recent.log
Weekly read-only gate-provenance audit output.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/learning-pi/e2e-*/
Per-run e2e artifacts: a result JSON and the session transcript per scenario,
plus a summary. The
.B lpi
opencode skill reads these for triage.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LEARNING_PI_ROOT
Override the learning-pi checkout root.
.TP
.B PI_OFFLINE
When set, the launcher's background availability check is skipped.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pi (1)
.PP
.I ~/learning-pi/CONTRACT.md
and
.I ~/learning-pi/README.md
document the behavior the gate protects and the revise door for intentional
behavior changes.
